23:24-08:00","id":1292586,"title":"","content":"So one last question, does that mean a wood aspect\u2019s anima banner triggers poison on withering damage? Or only on a crashed target where they recieve lethal? I\u2019m assuming withering triggers it, but only when damage is actually dealt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:37:26-08:00","id":1292591,"title":"","content":"The wood anima does also trigger on withering damage, yes. Since it specifies that it triggers on damage, not necessary lethal damage. (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1210062#post1210062\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...62#post1210062</a>)<br /> <br /> So your assumption would be correct. It triggers, but only when damage is actually dealt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":2272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","user":"senresk","date":". 02-27-2019, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T14:08:49-08:00","id":1292602,"title":"","content":"Damn, this is pretty awesome. 